# Frontier Model Strengths: A Practitioner's Consensus
**March 2026 — Focused on Agent Orchestration & Large-Scale Engineering**

---

## The Current Field

The frontier as of March 2026 consists of five meaningful contenders:

- **Claude Opus 4.6** (Anthropic, Feb 2026) — 1M context (beta), 80.8% SWE-bench, extended thinking, context compaction, agent teams
- **GPT-5.4** (OpenAI, Mar 2026) — 1M context in Codex mode, native computer use, 75.1% Terminal-Bench, tool search with 47% token reduction
- **GPT-5.2 / o3-pro** (OpenAI) — Still the general API flagship; o3-pro for maximum reasoning compute
- **Gemini 3.1 Pro** (Google, Feb 2026) — 1M production context, 77.1% ARC-AGI-2, 94.3% GPQA Diamond, $2/$12 pricing
- **Grok 4** (xAI) — Four parallel agents architecture; surprise entrant on WebDev Arena
- Notable open-weight: **DeepSeek-V3**, **GLM-4.7 Thinking** (90%+ Terminal-Bench Hard), **MiniMax M2.5** (80.2% SWE-bench at $0.30/$1.20)

**Key meta-finding**: No single model dominates. The frontier has fragmented by *task type*. The consensus among serious practitioners is multi-model routing, not single-model loyalty.

